{
  "_README": [
    "Single source of truth for every product on the site. Edit this file and reload — nothing about",
    "stock, sizes, photos or copy is hardcoded in script.js any more.",
    "",
    "FIELDS (per product):",
    "  id           stable slug, never reuse or change one — carts, click stats and a future admin",
    "               dashboard key off it. Renaming a product is fine; changing its id is not.",
    "  name         display name. Must stay UNIQUE: the cart, click tracking and pricing.json all",
    "               key on it.",
    "  brand        designer name shown above every title. Use \"[brand?]\" when unknown — it renders",
    "               in warning orange so an unlabelled piece can't pass as a finished listing.",
    "  category     must appear in the `categories` list below.",
    "  description  one short line, shown on the card and in the modal.",
    "  image        main photo, repo-relative path.",
    "  images       additional photos, same form. Empty today; a gallery is not built yet, so",
    "               anything added here is stored but not yet displayed.",
    "  retailPrice  single-unit price.",
    "  bulkPrice    per-unit price at bulkMinQty and above, or null for no bulk discount.",
    "  bulkMinQty   units at which bulkPrice starts applying.",
    "  sizes        [{size, qty}] for EVERY size, including qty 0. Zero-qty sizes are kept here so",
    "               they can be restocked without retyping the size list; the site hides them.",
    "  status       \"available\" or \"sold\". \"sold\" disables Buy/Add-to-Cart and hides the count.",
    "               A product whose sizes are all 0 is treated as sold out regardless of status.",
    "  featured     true puts it in the fallback featured stack. Real visitor clicks still",
    "               outrank this — see renderFeatured().",
    "",
    "PRICING: pricing.json still owns the full quantity ladder and WINS wherever it has an entry.",
    "That file can express 4 tiers (1/5/10/20 for shirts); retailPrice+bulkPrice here can express",
    "one break. The two are consistent today. If you add a product here with no pricing.json entry,",
    "retailPrice/bulkPrice/bulkMinQty are used on their own, so new products price correctly without",
    "touching that file."
  ],
